WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.875 --> 00:00:16.305
It was a normal November morning—except for one thing.

2
00:00:17.926 --> 00:00:19.768
Everyone was upset about something.

3
00:00:20.889 --> 00:00:22.930
My brother, Tate, was upset because of me.

4
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:26.033
"Mom!" Tate yelled.

5
00:00:26.053 --> 00:00:29.676
"I found more of Iggy's junk in my closet!"

6
00:00:31.324 --> 00:00:33.666
I had moved into my own room a while ago.

7
00:00:34.927 --> 00:00:36.768
I guess I'd left some stuff behind.

8
00:00:36.788 --> 00:00:39.370
"Tell him to get it out of here!"

9
00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:40.530
Tate complained.

10
00:00:42.872 --> 00:00:44.293
My mom walked into my room.

11
00:00:44.313 --> 00:00:50.137
"Iggy, please clean your stuff out of Tate's closet today after school," she said.

12
00:00:51.118 --> 00:00:52.779
Suddenly she looked around my room.

13
00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.781
Then she got upset.

14
00:00:56.801 --> 00:01:00.424
"And clean your own room, Iggy!"

15
00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:01.440
she added.

16
00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:03.101
"It's a mess!"

17
00:01:04.462 --> 00:01:06.063
Of course my room is a mess.

18
00:01:07.024 --> 00:01:10.186
It's the room of a brilliant inventor—me, Iggy!

19
00:01:11.026 --> 00:01:13.347
Brilliant people always have messy rooms.

20
00:01:14.248 --> 00:01:18.891
I bet Thomas Edison, who invented the light bulb, had a super messy room.

21
00:01:20.051 --> 00:01:22.513
And I bet his mom didn't tell him to clean it up!

22
00:01:23.493 --> 00:01:27.996
She probably knew that he was busy thinking up clever new inventions, just like me.

23
00:01:29.512 --> 00:01:33.416
That morning I walked to school with my friends Molly, Josh, and Jenny.

24
00:01:34.316 --> 00:01:35.778
And Molly was upset too.

25
00:01:37.039 --> 00:01:38.960
She told us why as we walked along.

26
00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:44.044
"My mom hired a babysitter for Caswell and me," she said.

27
00:01:44.064 --> 00:01:47.948
"Mom wanted some time to meet a friend or go shopping."

28
00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:50.350
"That's great," I said.

29
00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:53.933
"Meeting a friend always puts my mom in a good mood."

30
00:01:53.953 --> 00:01:57.696
"But you don't understand," said Molly.

31
00:01:58.656 --> 00:02:00.877
"I don't like Lucy, our new babysitter."

32
00:02:02.177 --> 00:02:04.918
"Is she mean, like a wicked stepmother?"

33
00:02:05.418 --> 00:02:06.278
asked Jenny.

34
00:02:07.339 --> 00:02:09.559
Jenny's class was reading fairy tales.

35
00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:13.681
Fairy tales have lots of wicked stepmothers in them.

36
00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:17.862
"No, Lucy is not mean," said Molly.

37
00:02:17.882 --> 00:02:20.042
"Why don't you like her then?"

38
00:02:20.523 --> 00:02:21.363
asked Josh.

39
00:02:21.383 --> 00:02:27.174
"Well," said Molly, "she talks on her cell phone a lot.

40
00:02:27.474 --> 00:02:31.598
And she and Caswell watch the TV show Monster Madness every day."

41
00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:35.341
"That sounds like fun," I said.

42
00:02:35.361 --> 00:02:40.205
"My mom won't let Tate and me watch any TV after school."

43
00:02:41.366 --> 00:02:45.330
"Monster Madness is a pretty scary show," said Molly.

44
00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:50.194
"Even when I'm in my room, I can still hear the monsters roaring.

45
00:02:50.854 --> 00:02:52.376
Now I can't sleep at night!"

46
00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:58.222
"Why don't you just ask Lucy if you can watch something else?"

47
00:02:58.523 --> 00:02:58.923
I said.

48
00:02:58.943 --> 00:03:01.445
"No way!"

49
00:03:01.845 --> 00:03:02.726
Molly replied.

50
00:03:02.746 --> 00:03:06.248
"Lucy and Caswell would think I'm a big baby.

51
00:03:06.748 --> 00:03:10.211
Caswell is much younger than I am, and he's not scared at all!"

52
00:03:12.733 --> 00:03:17.256
That morning Molly yawned at least ten times during social studies.

53
00:03:20.358 --> 00:03:22.459
"Molly," said our teacher, Mrs.

54
00:03:22.539 --> 00:03:27.255
Romano. "What did Egyptian children do in their spare time?"

55
00:03:28.336 --> 00:03:33.680
"Sleep?" said Molly, yawning again.

56
00:03:35.061 --> 00:03:39.185
Everyone laughed, except for Mrs.

57
00:03:39.265 --> 00:03:40.186
Romano and me.

58
00:03:41.227 --> 00:03:44.529
Mrs. Romano seemed annoyed that Molly wasn't paying attention.

59
00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:48.833
And I was a little worried about our language arts project.

60
00:03:49.914 --> 00:03:52.096
Soon we were going to start writing books.

61
00:03:53.684 --> 00:03:58.288
Molly and I were partners, so I needed her to be alert and wide-awake.

62
00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:03.952
On the way home after school we passed Bubbles Bath Shop.

63
00:04:05.193 --> 00:04:08.176
Josh and Jenny's dad had recently gotten a job there.

64
00:04:09.317 --> 00:04:10.838
We stopped and looked in the window.

65
00:04:11.779 --> 00:04:16.322
A sign read "Bathe Your Worries Away In A Relaxing Bubble Bath!"

66
00:04:16.342 --> 00:04:22.888
"Bubbles Bath Shop sells lots of different kinds of bubble bath soap," said Jenny.

67
00:04:24.064 --> 00:04:27.645
"Chocolate, strawberry, and even bubble gum," added Josh.

68
00:04:28.986 --> 00:04:31.827
Suddenly I got an idea for a new invention.

69
00:04:33.227 --> 00:04:35.888
It was an invention that would help Molly relax.

70
00:04:37.889 --> 00:04:41.170
It might also keep my mom and Tate from getting upset with me.

71
00:04:42.471 --> 00:04:45.472
Now that would really be a great invention!
